WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.340
Picture a remote mining town
with just one big employer.

2
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:06.540
The firm could hire one more worker,

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.350
who would add 15 dollars to its sales.

4
00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:12.240
That worker would be paid just 14 dollars.

5
00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.830
Yet the firm says no. Why would it turn

6
00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:17.860
away a worker who adds
more than their wage?

7
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.680
In this mission, you'll build
the diagram for a market

8
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.660
with only one buyer of labour,

9
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.150
step by step.

10
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.900
Then you'll choose how
many workers the firm hires

11
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.600
in a graph lab, and test your choice.

12
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.720
Your mission: find out why
one big employer can say no.
